hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"989","Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dhabi informed us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, informed us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: They mentioned their negligence in sleeping, and he said: They slept, even when the sun rose, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no negligence in sleeping. Negligence is only in vigilance, so if one of you forgets a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it, and at its time the next day.” Abdullah bin Rabah said: Imran heard me narrating the hadith, and he said: O boy, look at how you narrate, for I witnessed the hadith with the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not deny anything of his hadith."
"990","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Thabit, he heard Abdullah bin Rabah speaking, on the authority of Abu Qatada, that when the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his companions fell asleep and missed the prayer, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Pray it until tomorrow.” ""Immediately"""
